      "question_id": "#77",
      "topic_id": 1,
      "course_id": 1,
      "case_study_id": null,
      "lab_id": 0,
      "question_text": "<p>A company uses AWS Organizations with all features enabled. The company has enabled AWS Security Hub in all member accounts and in all AWS Regions. The company has created a VPC in the eu-central-1 Region in a member AWS account.<br><br><br><br>A security engineer has verified that no security group rules in the VPC allow inbound traffic from all IP addresses on TCP port 22. The security engineer needs an automated system. The system must prevent the creation of security group rules in the VPC that allow traffic from all IP addresses on TCP port 22.<br><br><br><br>Which solution will meet these requirements?<br><br></p>",
      "mark": 1,
      "is_partially_correct": false,
      "question_type": "1",
      "difficulty_level": "0",
      "general_feedback": "<p><strong>✅ ĐÁP ÁN ĐÚNG</strong>: B</p><p><strong>🎯 ĐỀ ĐANG HỎI GÌ?</strong></p><ul><li>Tự động ngăn rule security group mở TCP 22 cho 0.0.0.0/0 trong một VPC.</li><li>Security Hub đã bật ở mọi account và Region.</li></ul><p><strong>💡 LÝ DO CHỌN ĐÁP ÁN</strong></p><p><strong>AWS Security Hub</strong> sinh finding khi có rule mở SSH ra toàn Internet. <strong>Amazon EventBridge</strong> bắt finding đó và gọi <strong>AWS Lambda</strong> để xoá rule vi phạm, hoàn toàn tự động.</p><p><strong>⚡ PHÂN TÍCH NHANH</strong></p><ul><li><strong>A</strong>: ❌ Chỉ cảnh báo qua SNS, không tự động xử lý.</li><li><strong>B</strong>: ✅ Security Hub finding → EventBridge → Lambda tự động remediate.</li><li><strong>C</strong>: ❌ <strong>SCP</strong> không có condition key để lọc theo CIDR/port của rule security group, nên không thể chặn chính xác như vậy.</li><li><strong>D</strong>: ❌ <strong>AWS Network Firewall</strong> lọc traffic, không ngăn tạo rule security group; không áp dụng được cho yêu cầu.</li></ul><p><strong>🔑 KEYWORDS CẦN NHỚ</strong></p><ul><li>Security Hub finding</li><li>EventBridge rule</li><li>Lambda auto-remediation</li><li>Security group 0.0.0.0/0 port 22</li></ul><p><strong>🧠 MẸO THI</strong></p><p>\"Gặp tự động remediate finding → nghĩ ngay đến Security Hub/Config + EventBridge + Lambda.\"</p>",
      "is_active": true,
      "answer_list": [
        {
          "question_answer_id": 1,
          "question_id": "#77",
          "answers": [
            {
              "choice": "<p>Enable an AWS CloudTrail organization trail that logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a CloudWatch alarm based on a log group metric filter. Configure the alarm to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when a security group rule is added that allows inbound traffic from all IP addresses. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.</p>",
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": ""
            },
            {
              "choice": "<p>Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that filters for Security Hub findings about security group rules that allow inbound traffic from all IP addresses on TCP port 22. Configure the EventBridge rule to target an AWS Lambda function that removes the unwanted security group rule.</p>",
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": ""
            },
            {
              "choice": "<p>Create an SCP that prevents the creation or modification of security group rules that allow inbound traffic from all IP addresses on TCP port 22.</p>",
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": ""
            },
            {
              "choice": "<p>Deploy AWS Network Firewall with a rule that inspects all inbound traffic and prevents incoming traffic on TCP port 22.</p>",
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "topic_name": "Exam AWS Certified Security - Specialty SCS-C03 topic 1 question 77 discussion - ExamTopics",
