          "id": 1758345,
          "date": "May 18, 2026 03:55 am",
          "username": "OCHT",
          "content": "Amazon OpenSearch Service (formerly Amazon Elasticsearch Service) is purpose-built for exactly this use case:<br/><br><br/><br>It can ingest logs from virtually all AWS services (CloudWatch Logs, CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, Application Load Balancer logs, etc.) in near real time.<br/><br>It offers powerful, full-text search capabilities via the OpenSearch API.<br/><br>OpenSearch Security Analytics allows you to create detection rules (including anomaly detection, threat detection, and custom correlation rules) and automatically trigger actions such as sending notifications to an Amazon SNS topic.<br/><br><br/><br>This combination satisfies all three requirements with a single, well-integrated service.",
